//! check: run(exit=0, stdout="7\n")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: conc.task.spawn, conc.task.scope, conc.chan.buf
//! s117 (#136): the shim travels with its spawner. A task entry is
//! reached by `func.addr`, not by a call, so before s117 the release
//! tier's partitioner (s43) saw no edge into the shim and bin-packed
//! it away from `main` — and the LLVM emitter then refused
//! `func.addr of @main.task0.entry outside this object's subset` on
//! a program the native tier runs (the issue's exact asymmetry; the
//! wolf-wws parked-forwarder shape, reduced). The two recursive
//! arithmetic mills below are the load-bearing filler: they push the
//! program past one cluster (post-opt WIR > cluster_target_size) and
//! recursion pins them against inlining, so the partition is real.
//! At base this file refused on --release and ran on --native; with
//! the v3 summary's `refs=` edge the shim is fused into its
//! spawner's cluster — unconditionally, even though `main`'s group
//! busts the size cap — and both lanes agree on exit 0.

